## Key notes (follow these so you don’t have to be asked again)

### Stack & structure
- **Next.js 16** App Router. Pages in `app/`, API routes in `app/api/`. Use `NextResponse.json()` in API routes.
- **Supabase**: `createSupabaseClient()` in client components (from `@/lib/supabase`). `createSupabaseServerClient()` in API routes and server code (from `@/lib/supabase-server`). Don’t mix them.
- **Styling**: Tailwind only. Use the `cn()` helper from `@/lib/utils` for conditional/merged class names. Reuse `components/ui/` (Button, Input, Label, Textarea, etc.) instead of rolling new primitives.
- **Icons**: `lucide-react`. **Toasts**: `sonner` (`toast.success`, `toast.error`, etc.).
- **Dates/times**: Use **Luxon** (`luxon`) for formatting and parsing. Time display: lowercase, no space (e.g. `8:00pm`), per `EventCard`’s `formatTime`.
- **Types**: `Event` and `Guest` live in `@/types/event`. Use these types; don’t redefine the same shapes elsewhere.

### Conventions
- **Formatting**: Match project Prettier: single quotes, print width 100, `arrowParens: "avoid"` (e.g. `x => x` not `(x) => x`), semicolons, trailing commas (ES5).
- **Components**: Default export for page and UI components. Add `'use client'` only when the component uses hooks, browser APIs, or client-only deps.
- **API routes**: Validate body/query, then get user with `supabase.auth.getUser()`. Return 400 for bad input, 401 when not authenticated, then do the work.
- **Forms**: React Hook Form in use (e.g. `EventForm`). Use existing form patterns and shared types for payloads.

### UI / copy
- **Location/address**: When showing an address without country, strip "United States" / "USA" (and "United", "States" as last two parts). See `addressWithoutCountry` in `EventCard`.
- **Guest names**: Prefer `first_name` / `last_name` where available; fall back to `name` or display logic already in the codebase.

### Commits
- When the user says "commit" (or similar): break changes into **focused chunks**—one logical change per commit—with **detailed, descriptive messages** (e.g. what changed and why). Don’t squash everything into a single commit unless the change is truly one unit of work.

